## Broken Access Control

## Summary
UnifiedTransform has a systemic broken access control vulnerability. This allows any authenticated user, regardless of role (including students), to tamper with academic records — promoting students, editing exam grading rules, modifying courses/sections, and creating/editing/deleting calendar events — and to view or edit other users' personal data via predictable ID enumeration (IDOR), including student/teacher profiles and class attendance rosters.

14 endpoints were confirmed vulnerable (see detailed list). Remediation requires consistently applying the existing permission middleware with correctly scoped abilities per action.


## Vulnerable Endpoints List
1. POST /promotions/promote
2. GET /promotions
3. POST /exams/edit-rule
4. POST /exams/grade/delete-rule
5. POST /school/course/update
6. POST /school/section/update
7. POST /teacher/update
8. POST /student/update
9. GET /students/edit/{id}
10. GET /teachers/edit/{id}
11. GET /teachers/view/profile/{id}
12. GET /attendances/view  (query params class_id/section_id/course_id)
13. GET /attendances/create  (take-attendance form)
14. POST /calendar-crud-ajax  (type=create/edit/delete)


## Impact
Any authenticated user (regardless of their role) can view and alter data of other users


